  "description": "We wish to add a conservation-style loft window to the front of your property. The proposed roof window is a VELUX Black (external) White (internal) Painted Conservation model, specifically designed for use in conservation areas or where planning guidance requires a traditional appearance. The window will be recessed into the roof to sit flush with the tiles and features a vertical central glazing bar. The external frame finish has been selected to match the colour of the surrounding roof tiles, ensuring minimal visual impact. The internal finish is white-painted, in keeping with the property’s interior style. The window is intended to bring natural light into a dark loft/landing/attic space and to allow for ventilation in an otherwise enclosed or poorly ventilated area. These improvements will enhance the ventilation of the house - it can get quite hot during the summer - while retaining the property's historic character. Please note that similar conservation-style roof windows have already been installed at Nos. 33–35 Grove Road, establishing a clear and appropriate local precedent. The proposed window will preserve the character and appearance of the street scene while offering improved ventilation and energy performance through modern double glazing and insulation. ",
